// TEST: Sqrt Odd Dimension Rejects (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3006
// ERROR-CONTAINS: unit dimension exponents are integers
// sqrt of an ODD-exponent unit has no representable signature: the answer is
// meters^(1/2) and the grammar carries integer exponents only. The arm used
// to answer "no signature", which is not the same as "dimensionless" -- an
// unconstrained result unifies with ANY unit, so `sqrt(m) + Float<seconds>`
// typechecked and silently produced a length-plus-time. Refusing here is the
// only answer that cannot be wrong.
Unit meters
Unit seconds
let d: Float<meters> = 4.0
let t: Float<seconds> = 1.0
let bad = sqrt(d) + t
